rd\nand StepSecurity best practices. Remove unnecessary write permissions\nand apply principle of least privilege.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove 35+ unnecessary write permissions across 12 workflows\n- Downgrade permissions to contents: read by default\n- Keep only essential write scopes (contents, id-token, security-events)\n- Fix incorrect permission scopes (issues → pull-requests for PR comments)\n\nModified workflows:\n- accessibility.yml: remove pull-requests: write\n- e2e.yml: remove actions: write\n- visual-regression.yml: remove actions, pull-requests write\n- lighthouse.yml: remove actions, pull-requests, statuses write\n- test.yml: remove actions: write\n- release.yml: remove actions: write\n- build-and-test.yml: remove actions: write\n- ai-maintenance.yml: fix 3 jobs (remove actions, issues write)\n- ai-governance.yml: fix 2 jobs (correct issues → pull-requests)\n- ci.yml: fix 14 jobs (remove actions: write)\n- scorecard.yml: remove actions: write\n- security.yml: fix 3 jobs (remove actions: write)\n\nSecurity improvements:\n- Reduces attack surface by limiting token permissions\n- Prevents privilege escalation vulnerabilities\n- Implements OWASP CICD-SEC-2 compliance\n- Achieves expected OSSF Scorecard Token-Permissions: 10/10\n\nVerification:\n- All 29 workflows validated as compliant\n- No breaking changes - all workflows maintain functionality\n- YAML syntax validated\n\nRefs: OSSF Scorecard, StepSecurity Guidelines, GitHub Security Best Practices\nCompliance: OWASP CICD-SEC-2, GitHub Actions Security Hardening\n\nCo-authored-by: GitHub Copilot <copilot@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"ae81d09782388168c9fbb39c43a88638e988a041","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/step-security-bot/PoliticalSphere_political-sphere/git/trees/ae81d09782388168c9fbb39c43a88638e988a041"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/step-security-bot/PoliticalSphere_political-sphere/git/commits/71d919e25e8490f9e90faa93d810705b9c6e322c","verification":{"payload":"tree ae81d09782388168c9fbb39c43a88