vernance (priority 2) - WCAG 2.2 AA accessibility, political neutrality, test quality\n  - Phase 4: Infrastructure (priority 3) - actionlint, hadolint, JSON/YAML validation\n\n- Enhanced commit message validation:\n  - Empty message detection\n  - Minimum 10 character requirement\n  - Conventional Commits enforcement\n  - WIP blocking on main branch\n  - Issue reference encouragement\n\n- Improved pre-push hooks:\n  - Full TypeScript type checking\n  - Changed file testing\n  - Security auditing (advisory)\n  - AI index updates\n  - Branch protection awareness (3-second warning for main)\n\n- Better developer experience:\n  - Clear, actionable error messages with recovery instructions\n  - Auto-fix with automatic staging\n  - File-specific globs to skip unnecessary checks\n  - Performance optimizations (parallel execution, incremental compilation)\n  - Professional output with emoji indicators and progress feedback\n\n- Comprehensive documentation:\n  - 1630-line implementation guide with exact code for all 8 phases\n  - Completion summary with verification results\n  - Rollback plan with timestamped backup\n  - Usage examples and troubleshooting\n\nCloses: Implementation of enhanced pre-commit hooks as specified\nSee: docs/05-engineering-and-devops/development/pre-commit-hooks-implementation-guide.md\nSee: docs/05-engineering-and-devops/development/pre-commit-hooks-IMPLEMENTATION-COMPLETE.md\n\n* test(hooks): validate enhanced pre-commit system\n\n* security: fix Scorecard pinned dependencies and token permissions issues\n\n- Pin npm dependencies to registry tarball URLs for exact hash pinning\n- Remove broad workflow permissions, add minimal job-level permissions\n- Use npm ci for reproducible installs with locked versions\n- Update corepack to use default pinned versions\n- Fix token permissions across all GitHub workflows\n\nResolves multiple Scorecard security alerts for pinned dependencies and token permissions.\n\n* feat(api): add fail-closed JSON body read timeout and enhanced startup logging\n\n- Add timeoutMs support to readJsonBody (default 10s, configurable via READ_BODY_TIMEOUT_MS)\n- Integrate timeout across auth/news routes in server.ts\n- Enhance startup logging with port, maxBodyBytes, bodyReadTimeoutMs, authImplementation metadata\n- Add body-timeout tests (2 passing) to validate timeout and success scenarios\n- Update TODO.md and CHANGELOG.md with new feature and security mitigation (slow-loris prevention)\n- Fix JudiciarySystem.tsx syntax errors (remove stray closing braces)\n- Fix .lefthook.yml accessibility hook configuration (use project ESLint config)\n- Prefix unused variables with underscore per project convention\n\nSecurity: Mitigates slow request body attacks (OWASP A01/A05).\nObservability: Enhanced startup logging improves traceability.\nTesting: 100% coverage for new timeout feature.\nDocs: backend.md update pending.\n\n* Initial plan (#122)\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update apps/web/src/components/Judiciary/JudiciarySystem.tsx\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update apps/web/src/components/Lobby.tsx\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: GitHub Copilot <copilot@example.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0fa92066bff9de94a673a60aefe7913860857c3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/step-security-bot/PoliticalSphere_political-sphere/git/trees/0fa92066bff9de94a673a60aefe7913860857c3e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/step-security-bot/PoliticalSphere_political-sphere/git/commits/6c8bdd31c812b03c9ff6b51af88320fc85e36115","verification":{"payload":"tree 0fa92066bff9de94a673a60aefe7913860857c3e\nparent 358d90c556233f1b4793025210eb8630d27314fc\nauthor PoliticalSphere <Morgan.Lowman@outlook.com> 1763399220 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1763399220 +0000\n\nfeat(api): Add fail-closed JSON body read timeout and enhanced startup logging (#121)\n\n* test(hooks): verify enhanced pre-commit validation system\n\n* feat(hooks): implement enhanced pre-commit validation system (v3.0.0)\n\n- Upgrade from Lefthook v2.0.0 to v3.0.0 with industry-standard patterns\n- Add centered Political Sphere ASCII logo banner (Phase 0)\n- Implement 4-layer validation architecture with priority execution:\n  - Phase 1: Security (priority 0) - gitleaks, dependency scanning, license check, env validation\n  - Phase 2: Code Quality (priority 1) - Biome/Prettier formatting, dual linting, incremental TypeScript\n  - Phase 3: Governance (priority 2) - WCAG 2.2 AA accessibility, political neutrality, test quality\n  - Phase 4: Infrastructure (priority 3) - actionlint, hadolint, JSON/YAML validation\n\n- Enhanced commit message validation:\n  - Empty message detection\n  - Minimum 10 character requirement\n  - Conventional Commits enforcement\n  - WIP blocking on main branch\n  - Issue reference encouragement\n\n- Improved pre-push hooks:\n  - Full TypeScript type checking\n  - Changed file testing\n  - Security auditing (advisory)\n  - AI index updates\n  - Branch protection awareness (3-second warning for main)\n\n- Better developer experience:\n  - Clear, actionable error messages with recovery instructions\n  - Auto-fix with automatic staging\n  - File-specific globs to skip unnecessary checks\n  - Performance optimizations (parallel execution, incremental compilation)\n  - Professional output with emoji indicators and progress feedback\n\n- Comprehensive documentation:\n  - 1630-line implementation guide with exact code for all 8 phases\n  - Completion summary with verification results\n  - Rollback plan with timestamped backup\n  - Usage examples and troubleshooting\n\nCloses: Implementation of enhanced pre-commit hooks as specified\nSee: docs/05-engineering-and-devops/development/pre-commit-hooks-implementation-guide.md\nSee: docs/05-engineering-and-devops/development/pre-commit-hooks-IMPLEMENTATION-COMPLETE.md\n\n* test(hooks): validate enhanced pre-commit system\n\n* security: fix Scorecard pinned dependencies and token permissions issues\n\n- Pin npm dependencies to registry tarball URLs for exact hash pinning\n- Remove broad workflow permissions, add minimal job-level permissions\n- Use npm ci for reproducible installs with locked versions\n- Update corepack to use default pinned versions\n- Fix token permissions across all GitHub workflows\n\nResolves multiple Scorecard security alerts for pinned dependencies and token permissions.\n\n* feat(api): add fail-closed JSON body read timeout and enhanced startup logging\n\n- Add timeoutMs support to readJsonBody (default 10s, configurable via READ_BODY_TIMEOUT_MS)\n- Integrate timeout across auth/news routes in server.ts\n- Enhance startup logging with port, maxBodyBytes, bodyReadTimeoutMs, authImplementation metadata\n- Add body-timeout tests (2 passing) to validate timeout and success scenarios\n- Update TODO.md and CHANGELOG.md with new feature and security mitigation (slow-loris prevention)\n- Fix JudiciarySystem.tsx syntax errors (remove stray closing braces)\n- Fix .lefthook.yml accessibility hook configuration (use project ESLint config)\n- Prefix unused variables with underscore per project convention\n\nSecurity: Mitigates slow request body attacks (OWASP A01/A05).\nObservability: Enhanced startup logging improves traceability.\nTesting: 100% coverage for new timeout feature.\nDocs: backend.md update pending.\n\n* Initial plan (#122)\n\nCo-authored-by: copilot-swe-agent[bot] <198982749+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update apps/web/src/components/Judiciary/JudiciarySystem.tsx\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* Update apps/web/src/components/Lobby.tsx\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <175728472+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------