thub.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Comprehensive platform upgrade - Database, Game Systems, CI/CD, and Quality Infrastructure (#106)\n\n* feat: major cleanup and game implementation improvements\n\n- Remove audit system artifacts and legacy scripts\n- Add complete game implementation (Parliament, Elections, Government, Judiciary, Media)\n- Implement WebSocket server with comprehensive testing\n- Add authentication components and user profile\n- Enhance AI governance workflows and monitoring\n- Add accessibility and visual regression testing\n- Implement contract testing and improved error handling\n- Add comprehensive API documentation (OpenAPI spec)\n- Remove deprecated audit trails and consolidate TODO tracking\n- Update project structure and dependencies\n- Add educational responsibility statement\n- Enhance CI/CD with new quality gates and workflows\n\nThis commit represents significant progress toward production-ready game platform with\nfull democratic simulation capabilities, security enhancements, and quality standards.\n\n* fix(database): standardize PostgreSQL setup and resolve seed issues\n\n- Fixed Prisma seed foreign key error by creating election before constituencies\n- Standardized local PostgreSQL port to 5433 (fallback when 5432 busy)\n- Removed duplicate DATABASE_URL from root .env to resolve Prisma conflict\n- Updated apps/api/.env and .env.example with correct connection strings\n- Added comprehensive database setup section to apps/api/README.md\n  - Docker and Homebrew installation instructions\n  - Seeding steps and troubleshooting guide\n  - Security warnings for credential rotation\n- Replaced any[] with unknown[] in seed script for lint compliance\n- Updated docs/TODO.md marking database setup tasks complete\n- Created ai-metrics directory to fix test failures\n\nDatabase now seeds successfully:\n- 2 chambers (Commons, Lords)\n- 1 demo election\n- 3 constituencies\n- 1 motion, press release, poll\n\nRefs #97\n\n* chore: fix linting errors and TypeScript deprecation warnings\n\n- Add ignoreDeprecations: 6.0 to tsconfig.json to silence baseUrl deprecation\n- Fix biome lint errors in tools/scripts/ai/pre-cache.js:\n  - Add node: protocol to Node.js builtin imports (fs, path, url)\n  - Remove implicit return values from forEach callbacks\n\nThese are code quality improvements that don''t affect functionality.","tree":{"sha":"afaffd4361609492a3dd7ae959c63298157dd814","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/step-security-bot/PoliticalSphere_political-sphere/git/trees/afaffd4361609492a3dd7ae959c63298157dd814"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/step-security-bot/PoliticalSphere_political-sphere/git/commits/fd3d42396ff72571f7cef4ba51c82231f9462ff9","verification":{"payload":"tree afaffd4361609492a3dd7ae959c63298157dd814\nparent 376664ee39591347ea4af66c5ef3953b1ad40857\nauthor PoliticalSphere <Morgan.Lowman@outlook.com> 1763317253 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1763317253 +0000\n\nfeat: Comprehensive platform upgrade - Database, Game Systems, CI/CD, and Quality Infrastructure (#106)\n\n* feat: major cleanup and game implementation improvements\n\n- Remove audit system artifacts and legacy scripts\n- Add complete game implementation (Parliament, Elections, Government, Judiciary, Media)\n- Implement WebSocket server with comprehensive testing\n- Add authentication components and user profile\n- Enhance AI governance workflows and monitoring\n- Add accessibility and visual regression testing\n- Implement contract testing and improved error handling\n- Add comprehensive API documentation (OpenAPI spec)\n- Remove deprecated audit trails and consolidate TODO tracking\n- Update project structure and dependencies\n- Add educational responsibility statement\n- Enhance CI/CD with new quality gates and workflows\n\nThis commit represents significant progress toward production-ready game platform with\nfull democratic simulation capabilities, security enhancements, and quality standards.\n\n* fix(datab